 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to permitting the Albany Cemetery Association to file a\ncertificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation with the department\nof state",
    "basePrintNo": "S5939",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5939-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5939\n\nSPONSOR: ASHBY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to permitting the Albany Cemetery Association to file\na certificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation with the\ndepartment of state\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would authorize the secretary of state to accept for\nfiling from the Albany Cemetery Association, an application for a\ncertificate of amendment of certificate of incorporation pursuant to\nsection 803 of the not-for-profit corporation law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 would authorize the secretary of state to accept for filing\nfrom Albany Cemetery Association, located in the county of Albany, an\napplication for a certificate of amendment. The filing would be required\nwithin one year of the effective date of this act.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Albany Cemetery Association was created by a special act of the\nLegislature in 1841. The Legislature amended the Charter in 1869.\n\nThe Albany Cemetery Association has been a not-for-profit state regu-\nlated entity.\n\nSince the cemetery was created by a special act of the legislature, the\ndepartment of state does not have the corporation in its database of\ncorporations which prevents Albany Cemetery from filing any updates to\nits certificate of incorporation to comply with changes in the law. This\nsituation also means that since the corporation is not listed in state\ndatabases, lenders will not extend credit for equipment and the federal\ngovernment will not process veteran services payments without a valid\nstate corporate status in their vendor system (System for Award Manage-\nment (SAM).\n\nThis bill would allow Albany Cemetery Association to file a certificate\nof amendment of their special act certificate of incorporation with the\nsecretary of state to comply with changes in the not-for-profit corpo-\nration law. This bill would also affirm the not-for-profit status of the\norganization.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
